<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ish-bosheth</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ishbaal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ish-bosheth was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saul">Saul</a> who, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, became king of Israel after his father's death at Mount Gilboa, ruling the northern tribes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahanaim">Mahanaim</a> with the support of the commander Abner while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebron">Hebron</a>. After Abner went over to David, Ish-bosheth was murdered by two of his officers, leaving David king of all Israel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ish-bosheth.jpg" alt="Ish-bosheth" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ishbosheth_is_slain.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
